WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.140
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.240 --> 00:03.080
Can I keep my distance from you for a while?

3
00:04.480 --> 00:05.360
[DON’T PAINT TILL YOU FAINT. — DEAN]

4
00:07.760 --> 00:08.640
Miss you.

5
00:08.800 --> 00:09.920
Miss you, too.

6
00:09.960 --> 00:11.200
Your painting is very beautiful.

7
00:11.680 --> 00:12.320
It’s freaking stunning.

8
00:12.480 --> 00:16.600
I can’t be the same person who believed and painted because of you anymore.

9
00:16.960 --> 00:18.280
Because I’ve realized that

10
00:18.320 --> 00:21.280
I should dedicate myself to what truly matters in my life.

11
00:21.440 --> 00:23.200
I think we should go our separate ways, Mes.

12
00:24.040 --> 00:25.200
Can I stay over at your place tonight?

13
00:25.440 --> 00:26.880
Will you stop being so cute?

14
00:26.920 --> 00:29.200
If I were so crazy about you that I lost my mind, what would I do?

15
02:11.880 --> 02:12.880
Making rice porridge?

16
02:13.120 --> 02:14.400
Mm, yeah.

17
02:15.880 --> 02:17.040
I thought you only knew how to make steak.

18
02:17.520 --> 02:18.800
Come on. That’s an insult.

19
02:19.520 --> 02:20.920
Who eats steak for breakfast?

20
02:21.200 --> 02:24.200
In the morning, it’s got to be rice porridge or congee.

21
02:40.760 --> 02:42.079
Well? It’s good, so give me some credit.

22
02:43.800 --> 02:44.800
It’s all right.

23
02:47.040 --> 02:52.680
This rice porridge is made with riceberry and has dried shrimp and cuttlefish.

24
02:53.040 --> 02:54.440
You don’t find this everywhere.

25
02:54.480 --> 02:58.000
If you want more, you’ll have to come here for breakfast every morning.

26
02:58.480 --> 02:59.400
Here only.

27
03:01.640 --> 03:02.480
Nonsense.

28
03:03.680 --> 03:05.040
Who eats the same thing every morning?

29
03:08.600 --> 03:09.360
Go sit down.

30
03:14.800 --> 03:17.840
I’ll make coffee so you can’t accuse me of doing nothing.

31
03:19.360 --> 03:20.200
Okay.

32
03:43.280 --> 03:44.040
Smells good.

33
03:45.120 --> 03:46.680
What? I haven’t even showered yet.

34
03:46.800 --> 03:48.680
What? I meant the coffee.

35
04:04.280 --> 04:05.080
Tasty.

36
04:08.360 --> 04:09.360
You mean the coffee?

37
04:09.520 --> 04:10.400
Of course.

38
04:11.240 --> 04:13.680
Then what? What else would I mean?

39
04:19.560 --> 04:20.399
Nothing.

40
04:26.240 --> 04:28.480
The coffee you make tastes the best, though.

41
04:53.640 --> 04:55.600
Hey, Duen’s calling.

42
04:55.680 --> 04:56.840
Put her on speaker.

43
04:57.120 --> 04:57.840
Okay.

44
05:00.360 --> 05:00.720
Why are you calling

45
05:00.760 --> 05:03.080
(Dad was hospitalized last night. He needed emergency surgery.)

46
05:09.600 --> 05:10.680
So…

47
05:12.000 --> 05:13.080
Is he out of surgery now?

48
05:15.040 --> 05:16.240
(Dad’s gone, Dean.)

49
05:19.480 --> 05:22.400
(There were complications during the surgery.)

50
05:22.440 --> 05:23.960
(The doctors couldn’t save him.)

51
05:26.240 --> 05:27.400
(You should come home, Dean.)

52
05:59.760 --> 06:00.600
Where are the car keys?

53
06:00.720 --> 06:01.680
I can drive…

54
06:09.360 --> 06:10.800
I’ll ask Pun if he’s free to drive.

55
06:11.200 --> 06:14.920
If he’s not, we can get a car service and go see Duen first.

56
06:19.160 --> 06:19.960
Eat something first.

57
06:24.960 --> 06:26.240
There’s nothing we can do, even if we go now.

58
06:31.400 --> 06:32.560
You can’t think straight on an empty stomach.

59
06:37.800 --> 06:39.080
Aren’t you in a hurry to get home?

60
06:41.240 --> 06:41.960
Eat first.

61
06:43.560 --> 06:44.480
We’ll figure things out later.

62
07:13.400 --> 07:14.400
Do you want my help?

63
07:15.200 --> 07:15.920
It’s fine.

64
07:16.920 --> 07:18.080
I can manage.

65
07:25.200 --> 07:26.160
Just let me know what you decide.

66
07:28.520 --> 07:29.560
I can go with you.

67
07:32.960 --> 07:35.320
We’ve had our meal. How about some dessert?

68
07:47.680 --> 07:50.760
Uh… Let me just take you home.

69
08:03.080 --> 08:03.920
It’s all right.

70
08:05.960 --> 08:07.160
I can book a ride.

71
08:11.760 --> 08:13.440
You should hurry home.

72
08:16.680 --> 08:17.480
Mhm.

73
09:00.800 --> 09:09.000
[CHANTING AND CREMATION CEREMONY SCHEDULE] [DATES: 28, 29, 30 NOVEMBER 2026]

74
09:12.320 --> 09:14.600
[CHANTING AND CREMATION CEREMONY SCHEDULE] [DATES: 28, 29, 30 DECEMBER 2026]

75
09:15.160 --> 09:16.080
[YOU’VE POSTED THE WRONG MONTH.]

76
09:16.240 --> 09:17.320
[I’VE CORRECTED IT.]

77
09:28.240 --> 09:31.000
[DATES: 28, 29, 30 DECEMBER 2026]

78
09:42.280 --> 09:43.400
I talked to Ten.

79
09:43.760 --> 09:45.720
We’ll definitely attend the cremation ceremony.

80
09:46.600 --> 09:49.280
But we’ll only attend the final night of the funeral chanting.

81
09:49.480 --> 09:50.720
The final night?

82
09:52.120 --> 09:53.240
But there are five nights of ceremonies.

83
09:53.280 --> 09:54.720
(Ten is busy,)

84
09:55.640 --> 09:57.920
and we’re still not sure if the plans will change.

85
10:05.640 --> 10:06.600
Is something wrong?

86
10:09.080 --> 10:09.800
Nothing.

87
10:13.720 --> 10:15.280
Let’s have dinner together, then.

88
10:16.800 --> 10:17.720
(I’ll see you.)

89
10:21.880 --> 10:22.560
Okay.

90
10:30.000 --> 10:31.000
Who was that?

91
10:31.480 --> 10:32.600
It’s Moth.

92
10:33.080 --> 10:35.000
He was asking when we’d be attending Dean’s father’s funeral.

93
10:35.440 --> 10:37.080
I thought Moth had already gone with Dean.

94
10:38.280 --> 10:39.680
That’s how it’s supposed to be,

95
10:40.080 --> 10:43.480
but if things went that smoothly, they wouldn’t be this couple.

96
10:48.000 --> 10:51.000
Wow, this looks delicious.

97
10:51.280 --> 10:52.400
Ridiculous.

98
10:53.520 --> 10:55.080
How can raw chicken look delicious?

99
10:57.520 --> 10:58.360
Not the chicken.

100
10:59.680 --> 11:00.880
I meant you.

101
11:04.280 --> 11:05.280
Shut up.

102
11:06.000 --> 11:06.880
What kind of joke is that?

103
11:07.880 --> 11:09.000
Just kidding.

104
11:09.880 --> 11:11.920
Why are you making so much? Can we finish all this?

105
11:13.000 --> 11:16.480
It’s not all for today. I’m keeping some in the fridge.

106
11:16.800 --> 11:19.280
When you’re busy with work and don’t have time to eat out,

107
11:19.600 --> 11:23.400
just take some out and pop it in the air fryer. It’ll be ready in no time.

108
11:24.080 --> 11:27.400
Oh, and there’s also some mixed vegetable stew in the fridge.

109
11:27.880 --> 11:30.280
Just heat it up whenever you’re hungry.

110
11:30.800 --> 11:36.400
Don’t let me catch you skipping meals because you’re too busy working again.

111
11:38.880 --> 11:39.800
Yes, sir.

112
11:40.040 --> 11:41.080
Roger that.

113
11:42.720 --> 11:43.400
Whoa.

114
11:44.080 --> 11:47.280
Whose boyfriend is this?

115
11:47.520 --> 11:50.000
So caring. How sweet!

116
11:51.760 --> 11:53.280
But you need to take care of yourself, too.

117
11:53.800 --> 11:55.320
You can’t always rely on me to look after you.

118
12:05.280 --> 12:05.960
Hey.

119
12:06.280 --> 12:09.480
There. A little reward for cooking for me.

120
12:10.480 --> 12:12.320
Not enough? Want another?

121
12:13.400 --> 12:14.680
Here I go!

122
12:40.200 --> 12:41.800
Ten will attend the funeral today,

123
12:42.400 --> 12:44.040
but he won’t be able to make it again after that.

124
12:45.840 --> 12:47.000
Work’s been hectic for him.

125
12:47.920 --> 12:50.120
His client just moved up the deadline.

126
12:51.080 --> 12:54.000
He asked you to pass on his condolences to Dean.

127
12:55.080 --> 12:57.880
I don’t even know when I’ll go myself.

128
13:01.280 --> 13:05.000
Besides, Dean never asked me to come.

129
13:05.280 --> 13:06.480
Are you crazy, Moth?

130
13:08.080 --> 13:09.800
Who asks someone to come to a funeral?

131
13:12.680 --> 13:14.480
You can go whenever you want.

132
13:14.840 --> 13:16.600
But does he want me there?

133
13:18.200 --> 13:19.200
I mean,

134
13:21.200 --> 13:25.680
would I even be able to help him, or would I just make him feel worse?

135
13:28.600 --> 13:30.080
Why would you think that?

136
13:36.200 --> 13:36.880
I don’t know.

137
13:40.280 --> 13:41.400
You know what?

138
13:43.000 --> 13:47.680
I was with him when he found out.

139
13:51.480 --> 13:53.080
And I had no freaking idea what to do.

140
13:55.040 --> 14:02.000
Dean was going through such a tough time, and all I did...

141
14:04.280 --> 14:09.080
All I did was stand there and sit there like an idiot.

142
14:11.760 --> 14:13.280
I didn’t know the right thing to say.

143
14:14.400 --> 14:19.000
I wanted to comfort him, but I didn’t know how.

144
14:22.000 --> 14:25.800
Damn. The more I talk about it, the more pathetic I feel.

145
14:26.160 --> 14:27.200
Hey, don’t say that.

146
14:29.200 --> 14:30.400
Don’t think of it that way.

147
14:31.440 --> 14:32.680
I don’t think Dean minded.

148
14:33.400 --> 14:34.840
But I was there.

149
14:38.520 --> 14:41.800
I was right there, so why did I...

150
14:48.000 --> 14:49.080
Listen to me.

151
14:50.760 --> 14:53.600
Just being there for him was enough.

152
14:56.240 --> 14:57.400
As for everything else,

153
14:58.280 --> 15:02.280
maybe you’re just not used to dealing with these things yet.

154
15:03.200 --> 15:07.480
Try a little harder, and you’ll get better at it.

155
15:23.120 --> 15:27.000
[ KITIPHON KITPHONKUN, AGE 66 8 JUL 1960 - 28 DEC 2026 ]

156
15:31.720 --> 15:34.000
Things are going to get better.

157
16:00.800 --> 16:01.480
What’s up?

158
16:03.200 --> 16:04.160
How are you holding up?

159
16:07.000 --> 16:08.400
I’m…

160
16:09.720 --> 16:10.600
a little busy.

161
16:12.600 --> 16:14.000
(Duen’s taken care of everything.)

162
16:14.320 --> 16:18.480
From finding a caterer to hiring a florist.

163
16:20.280 --> 16:21.400
From start to finish.

164
16:24.720 --> 16:25.880
Do you want me there with you?

165
16:35.680 --> 16:36.200
Mm.

166
16:37.480 --> 16:38.280
Come.

167
16:43.160 --> 16:44.200
I’ll be there tomorrow.

168
16:46.320 --> 16:48.880
How are you getting here?

169
16:49.800 --> 16:52.400
I’ll figure it out. Don’t worry.

170
16:53.200 --> 16:57.400
Take a van to the provincial bus terminal,

171
16:58.400 --> 17:02.800
then book a ride to Duen’s café.

172
17:04.000 --> 17:04.800
Okay.

173
17:07.880 --> 17:08.599
So…

174
17:10.599 --> 17:12.200
Are you taking the earliest van?

175
17:14.200 --> 17:16.280
Mm-hmm, the earliest one.

176
17:22.880 --> 17:23.680
Okay.

177
19:06.800 --> 19:08.080
Duen’s still keeping her café open?

178
19:09.000 --> 19:11.880
I thought she’d be busy with the funeral arrangements.

179
19:13.600 --> 19:16.000
Yeah. She has plenty of employees.

180
19:17.600 --> 19:18.680
They can help out.

181
19:19.240 --> 19:21.800
Closing the café would mean losing income.

182
19:22.920 --> 19:24.120
Life has to go on.

183
19:32.080 --> 19:33.200
What are you doing?

184
19:34.600 --> 19:35.680
Dressing up the cat?

185
19:36.520 --> 19:37.080
Look.

186
19:37.880 --> 19:38.800
How cute!

187
19:48.600 --> 19:49.440
This one’s cute, too.

188
19:50.560 --> 19:51.000
Oh.

189
19:55.080 --> 19:56.200
It kind of looks like you.

190
19:57.080 --> 19:57.800
Which part?

191
19:58.320 --> 19:59.240
Every part.

192
20:03.080 --> 20:03.880
Fine, it does.

193
20:39.600 --> 20:41.040
[CHANTING AND CREMATION CEREMONY SCHEDULE]

194
20:41.040 --> 20:42.600
Hi, Moth. You’re here.

195
20:43.880 --> 20:44.720
Good evening.

196
20:46.400 --> 20:47.680
My deepest condolences.

197
20:48.600 --> 20:49.640
Thank you.

198
20:50.000 --> 20:51.800
Let me take you to pay your respects.

199
20:52.400 --> 20:53.680
It’s okay, Mom.

200
20:54.000 --> 20:55.880
I can take him. Don’t worry.

201
20:59.080 --> 20:59.680
Come on.

202
22:07.080 --> 22:09.160
Here, Moth. Take some fish maw soup.

203
22:09.320 --> 22:10.240
We have plenty left.

204
22:10.600 --> 22:12.440
Whoa, but I’ve already eaten.

205
22:12.880 --> 22:16.200
Go on, have some. Want some bread, too?

206
22:18.000 --> 22:18.920
I’m not going back just yet.

207
22:19.920 --> 22:22.680
I’m planning to stay one more day.

208
22:23.040 --> 22:23.680
Really, dear?

209
22:24.080 --> 22:26.960
You can stay at my house. I’ll make you something to eat.

210
22:28.520 --> 22:30.000
I remember you like spicy curry.

211
22:30.920 --> 22:31.840
I’ll be right back.

212
22:32.680 --> 22:33.040
Sure.

213
22:37.200 --> 22:38.120
That’s just how she is.

214
22:38.960 --> 22:40.160
Just humor her.

215
22:40.480 --> 22:41.520
She likes taking care of people.

216
22:42.240 --> 22:43.720
She worries about everyone.

217
22:45.120 --> 22:48.240
That’s why she stayed with Dad for so long. He liked being taken care of, too.

218
22:50.680 --> 22:52.320
I figured as much.

219
22:53.200 --> 22:56.960
She must have a lot more free time now, with no one to look after.

220
22:58.880 --> 23:00.880
She still has Dean.

221
23:02.320 --> 23:04.600
Oh, him.

222
23:05.720 --> 23:07.240
Mom doesn’t want to move to Bangkok.

223
23:08.920 --> 23:12.160
Besides, Dean has you taking care of him.

224
23:16.320 --> 23:16.880
No.

225
23:19.280 --> 23:22.600
Dean never asks for much.

226
23:24.560 --> 23:27.840
I know, deep down, Dean is a lot like Dad.

227
23:29.160 --> 23:30.040
He’s tight-lipped.

228
23:30.520 --> 23:32.880
He acts nonchalant, like he doesn’t care.

229
23:33.800 --> 23:36.320
But deep inside, he’s very sensitive.

230
23:38.240 --> 23:39.440
He likes to act tough,

231
23:39.760 --> 23:44.120
but what he really wants is someone who pays attention to him.

232
23:47.040 --> 23:50.760
I was so afraid no one would ever understand him.

233
23:51.880 --> 23:54.160
But seeing you here puts my mind at ease.

234
24:02.760 --> 24:05.080
Please take care of my little brother.

235
24:12.920 --> 24:14.480
You’re done for.

236
24:18.320 --> 24:19.880
I’m not going easy. I’m warning you.

237
24:20.320 --> 24:22.560
Whoa, he’s taking all the money!

238
24:44.000 --> 24:45.120
Are these pictures for your content?

239
24:46.520 --> 24:46.960
No.

240
24:47.880 --> 24:48.800
Just keeping them in my collection.

241
24:50.760 --> 24:51.400
I’m used to taking pictures.

242
24:52.840 --> 24:53.800
Let me take some of you, too.

243
24:54.560 --> 24:55.360
The view is beautiful.

244
24:56.200 --> 24:56.720
No.

245
24:57.800 --> 24:58.720
Come on. Just a few.

246
25:01.760 --> 25:02.600
Why so close?

247
25:03.880 --> 25:04.840
I can zoom out.

248
25:07.040 --> 25:07.960
Smile.

249
25:09.200 --> 25:09.880
Enough.

250
25:11.000 --> 25:11.880
Why taking so many pictures?

251
25:13.920 --> 25:14.560
Where should we go next?

252
25:15.520 --> 25:16.800
How about the market near the temple?

253
25:22.400 --> 25:23.240
Aren’t you sad at all?

254
25:29.200 --> 25:29.720
You think…

255
25:32.840 --> 25:34.120
I should be sadder?

256
25:39.080 --> 25:39.480
No.

257
25:41.600 --> 25:42.720
That’s not what I meant.

258
25:46.680 --> 25:48.960
Everyone copes in their own way.

259
26:00.520 --> 26:05.720
Then I guess this is the saddest face I can make.

260
26:11.520 --> 26:12.720
Were you close to your dad?

261
26:15.720 --> 26:16.200
No.

262
26:19.720 --> 26:20.760
Well, we used to be.

263
26:21.960 --> 26:27.960
But after I moved out, we grew apart.

264
26:44.640 --> 26:46.680
Should we go back together?

265
26:47.600 --> 26:49.200
Sounds good. There’s nothing else to do here.

266
26:49.960 --> 26:50.280
Okay.

267
26:53.600 --> 26:53.840
Hey!

268
26:54.600 --> 26:55.120
What are you doing here?

269
26:55.640 --> 26:56.800
Who are you paying your respects to, huh?

270
26:57.240 --> 26:57.800
Get out!

271
26:58.720 --> 27:00.240
The exit’s that way. Go!

272
27:00.400 --> 27:02.240
Can I say goodbye to him one last time?

273
27:02.400 --> 27:03.360
Say goodbye? Huh?

274
27:04.320 --> 27:06.440
Did you love each other so much that you had to say goodbye?

275
27:08.280 --> 27:08.800
Why?

276
27:09.120 --> 27:10.200
How dare you show your face here?

277
27:11.440 --> 27:13.840
You have no shame, do you?

278
27:14.720 --> 27:15.080
Dean.

279
27:15.480 --> 27:16.120
Leave now.

280
27:16.680 --> 27:17.960
Don’t ever show your face here again.

281
27:18.640 --> 27:19.320
Especially not to me.

282
27:20.160 --> 27:23.440
Don’t make me hate my dad

283
27:24.720 --> 27:25.960
or despise you two any more than I already do.

284
27:28.360 --> 27:28.640
Go.

285
27:29.400 --> 27:29.960
Dean.

286
27:31.400 --> 27:32.760
Moth, please take Dean away.

287
27:33.400 --> 27:33.880
Of course, ma’am.

288
27:35.560 --> 27:36.000
Come on.

289
28:33.000 --> 28:33.680
Thanks.

290
28:38.440 --> 28:39.320
Have some sugar.

291
28:41.320 --> 28:42.680
It might make you feel better.

292
28:54.480 --> 28:57.120
Have you ever felt like you couldn’t breathe,

293
28:59.000 --> 29:01.440
like the whole world was crumbling beneath your feet?

294
29:06.440 --> 29:07.120
No.

295
29:14.160 --> 29:14.840
I have.

296
29:21.360 --> 29:22.960
When I found out Dad was having an affair.

297
29:29.360 --> 29:29.920
It’s funny.

298
29:31.600 --> 29:33.200
I used to think Mom and Dad were in love.

299
29:37.160 --> 29:40.320
I saw them hug and say they loved each other every day.

300
29:43.880 --> 29:45.200
But when I was in junior high,

301
29:47.760 --> 29:49.560
I started noticing that Dad was acting weird.

302
29:52.000 --> 29:52.800
So I followed him.

303
29:57.520 --> 29:59.000
I saw him with another woman.

304
30:02.480 --> 30:04.200
He had a whole other life I knew nothing about.

305
30:06.360 --> 30:07.480
Dad used to be my hero.

306
30:11.280 --> 30:14.000
After that, all I saw was a liar.

307
30:22.600 --> 30:26.240
Hugs weren’t expressions of love.

308
30:33.360 --> 30:34.440
They were expressions of guilt.

309
30:38.880 --> 30:40.120
The love within my family,

310
30:41.960 --> 30:45.120
I couldn’t even tell if it was real or fake.

311
30:52.160 --> 30:53.120
That’s why I hated coming home.

312
30:54.840 --> 30:55.840
Everything felt like a sham.

313
30:58.480 --> 31:02.400
I felt bad for Mom and Duen. They always had to take care of Dad.

314
31:05.960 --> 31:07.560
That’s why I don’t like getting attached to anyone.

315
31:09.600 --> 31:13.960
I’m afraid I’ll turn out to be a liar just like Dad someday.

316
31:21.120 --> 31:22.280
That has nothing to do with you.

317
31:26.880 --> 31:30.840
I believe you’d never be like that.

318
31:50.000 --> 31:53.160
Actually, I don’t think you should waste your time on me.

319
31:57.320 --> 31:57.840
What?

320
32:00.560 --> 32:06.040
Because the truth is, our relationship is a lie, too.

321
32:08.200 --> 32:09.280
Just like the story about my dad I just told you.

322
32:13.400 --> 32:14.360
It’s different.

323
32:14.400 --> 32:14.800
It’s the same.

324
32:16.280 --> 32:20.280
I hit on you because I wanted to give Ten a chance to pursue Pun.

325
32:21.440 --> 32:22.000
And you.

326
32:23.120 --> 32:27.680
You agreed to be with me because you wanted Pun to move on from you, right?

327
32:32.280 --> 32:33.840
We’ve just been using each other as pawns.

328
32:34.760 --> 32:35.080
Right?

329
32:38.560 --> 32:39.800
Why are you bringing this up now?

330
32:39.920 --> 32:40.960
Because now’s the best time to face it.

331
32:44.560 --> 32:47.760
Why don’t we just admit the truth and go our separate ways?

332
32:53.040 --> 32:58.080
That’s better than… lying to each other until we die.

333
33:05.160 --> 33:06.160
Are you breaking up with me?

334
33:09.000 --> 33:09.440
I don’t know.

335
33:11.840 --> 33:13.000
Can we even call it a breakup...

336
33:17.360 --> 33:21.600
when we were never really together in the first place?

337
33:43.640 --> 33:44.280
Okay.

338
34:11.360 --> 34:12.199
Should we go back to your place?

339
34:14.320 --> 34:15.400
To finish it?

340
34:16.040 --> 34:16.719
No need.

341
34:17.080 --> 34:17.760
It’s already over.

342
34:18.239 --> 34:19.239
(But we already have plans.)

343
34:19.239 --> 34:19.960
Don’t be silly.

344
34:20.239 --> 34:21.040
Is he really just a senior?

345
34:21.920 --> 34:23.120
You guys talked for an hour.

346
34:23.520 --> 34:25.560
If you’re going to be like this, then I don’t want to talk.

347
34:26.520 --> 34:28.480
Didn’t you hear that he invited me too?

348
34:29.040 --> 34:32.480
If you f*cking come, I’ll hate you for the rest of my life.

349
34:44.800 --> 34:45.920
Hey, Moth. Where is Dean?

350
34:46.639 --> 34:48.040
I don’t know. I’m leaving.

351
35:42.200 --> 35:42.920
Dean.

352
35:43.800 --> 35:45.360
You shouldn’t have done that.

353
35:47.080 --> 35:49.720
What am I supposed to do to make everyone happy?

354
35:51.480 --> 35:55.200
Should I just pretend I don’t know anything, like I used to?

355
36:00.680 --> 36:03.560
I settled things with your dad a long time ago.

356
36:11.160 --> 36:13.400
Nobody’s perfect, Dean.

357
36:15.360 --> 36:18.360
Your dad couldn’t turn back time and undo what he’d done.

358
36:21.800 --> 36:25.280
But he’d proved that he’d chosen not to let go of my hand.

359
36:34.040 --> 36:35.840
And I forgave him.

360
37:13.600 --> 37:16.720
That woman started a new family a long time ago.

361
37:18.200 --> 37:20.080
She just wanted to bid Dad farewell today.

362
37:25.400 --> 37:27.720
Everyone has moved on.

363
37:32.400 --> 37:35.240
I won’t blame you if you can’t forgive Dad,

364
37:37.360 --> 37:41.600
but don’t hold on to it so tightly that you become afraid to let yourself love someone.

365
37:45.120 --> 37:51.360
Dean, you truly deserve to be with someone who loves you.

366
38:52.320 --> 38:52.920
Hello.

367
38:53.760 --> 38:54.960
What did you and Dean fight about?

368
38:57.080 --> 38:58.360
Word got to you fast.

369
38:59.640 --> 39:03.840
(Ohm and Boom were worried about you, so they texted me.)

370
39:05.440 --> 39:07.440
So, what’s going on?

371
39:09.080 --> 39:09.880
I’m going crazy, that’s what!

372
39:11.120 --> 39:12.680
Being with someone like him is driving me freaking crazy.

373
39:20.800 --> 39:21.960
I think I’ve had enough.

374
39:24.840 --> 39:26.640
Why do you guys have to make everything so difficult?

375
39:27.480 --> 39:28.360
I don’t get it.

376
39:29.880 --> 39:31.400
(Other people aren’t like this.)

377
39:31.920 --> 39:35.320
Maybe things would be easier if he weren’t in my life.

378
39:36.040 --> 39:39.760
I mean, you should keep things simple.

379
39:40.480 --> 39:41.440
Just be straightforward.

380
39:42.360 --> 39:43.480
How am I difficult?

381
39:44.120 --> 39:44.840
(Everything is difficult with you.)

382
39:45.920 --> 39:47.160
(Both you and Dean.)

383
39:47.560 --> 39:48.640
(You two are so difficult.)

384
39:53.680 --> 39:58.000
(Can’t you just accept how you feel and be honest with each other?)

385
39:59.280 --> 40:00.680
It might be hard at first,

386
40:03.080 --> 40:05.840
but trust me, you can do it.

387
40:11.240 --> 40:16.480
What happened today alone hurt so much I almost lost my mind.

388
40:18.200 --> 40:23.040
(But no matter how much it hurts, you still love him, right?)

389
41:07.800 --> 41:09.200
[I’M HIS ONLY SON. ]

390
41:09.200 --> 41:11.080
[…FOR BEING HERE TO SEND HIM OFF ON HIS FINAL JOURNEY TODAY.]

391
41:11.080 --> 41:12.280
[HE WAS LOVED BY HIS FAMILY.]

392
41:23.960 --> 41:27.080
Honey. Look.

393
41:27.080 --> 41:28.600
It’s Dean.

394
41:28.600 --> 41:30.720
He hurried home to celebrate your birthday.

395
41:30.800 --> 41:32.600
He must have missed you so much.

396
41:34.120 --> 41:38.280
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

397
42:01.080 --> 42:10.640
[WE WEREN’T THAT CLOSE, BUT I STILL LOV…]

398
42:56.360 --> 42:58.400
On behalf of the Kitphonkun family,

399
43:00.360 --> 43:05.080
I, the only son, would like to thank you from the bottom of my heart

400
43:06.560 --> 43:10.240
for being here to send my dad off on his final journey today.

401
43:13.240 --> 43:23.440
Dad Kittiphon lived his life with love and made sacrifices for his family.

402
43:24.640 --> 43:27.160
He was the warmest, strongest shelter for…

403
43:28.680 --> 43:33.360
For all of us.

404
44:02.960 --> 44:04.920
Dad taught me the most important thing:

405
44:05.720 --> 44:10.520
to always give my best in everything I do.

406
44:13.040 --> 44:14.800
Show your greatest kindness to those you choose to be kind to.

407
44:16.560 --> 44:18.400
Give your greatest love to those you choose to love.

408
44:21.360 --> 44:22.560
Because life is short,

409
44:25.680 --> 44:27.240
and we never know when we’ll have to part ways.

410
44:54.360 --> 44:57.360
Dad began his career as a government official in…

411
44:59.880 --> 45:02.360
199… 3.

412
45:03.600 --> 45:04.400
I’m sorry.

413
45:05.600 --> 45:07.000
1987.

414
45:08.840 --> 45:10.840
And he continued working until his retirement.

415
45:39.520 --> 45:41.920
I know Dad was never much of a talker.

416
45:45.760 --> 45:47.400
But he taught me love.

417
45:48.720 --> 45:55.240
He gave Duen, Mom, and mewarmth and stability.

418
45:57.800 --> 45:59.000
They were priceless.

419
46:02.640 --> 46:07.600
He might not have said much, but all three of us could feel them.

420
46:11.880 --> 46:14.760
Even though he made mistakes

421
46:16.480 --> 46:20.400
and let people down,especially his own family,

422
46:25.960 --> 46:32.200
he taught me that nobody in this world is perfect.

423
46:35.760 --> 46:39.160
We just have to choose what we want to live with.

424
46:40.080 --> 46:44.800
Will we drown in guilt over the past, or find the courage to right our wrongs?

425
47:00.800 --> 47:01.560
Honey.

426
47:02.840 --> 47:04.080
Honey.

427
48:20.840 --> 48:24.760
(There may be a thousand reasons why people fall in love.)

428
48:27.280 --> 48:30.360
(Some reasons might even sound crazy.)

429
48:32.320 --> 48:33.240
It’s good.

430
48:33.440 --> 48:35.000
(But it’s when we’re going through our toughest times)

431
48:35.760 --> 48:39.200
(that we realize just how much the person in front of us means to us,)

432
48:42.400 --> 48:48.480
(and how much harder life would be without them.)

433
49:41.920 --> 49:43.440
You haven’t asked Moth to be your boyfriend yet?

434
49:43.760 --> 49:45.560
Moth and I are way past that point.

435
49:45.880 --> 49:48.000
Maybe Moth’s waiting for you to ask him.

436
49:48.520 --> 49:49.840
I’m applying for a scholarship in New York.

437
49:50.080 --> 49:50.840
Do you want to go?

438
49:54.200 --> 49:56.920
I’m afraid I’ll regret it for the rest of my life if I don’t go.

439
49:59.880 --> 50:00.680
Can you stay with me?

440
50:02.240 --> 50:04.280
I want to be honest with my heart.

441
50:04.560 --> 50:06.480
And don’t I have a place in your heart at all?

442
50:06.840 --> 50:09.800
Are you sure everything will stay the same?
